# Frontend standards

- Use React, TypeScript, Radix Primitives, and Tailwind.
- Do not use Redux or Redux Toolkit.
- Consider XState only for specific workflows where statecharts simplify
  transitions and testing; it is optional, not a required global store.
- Keep components small and focused. Extract repeated controls and style variants.
- Use shared semantic color tokens such as `bg-surface`, `text-content`,
  `border-outline`, and `text-danger`. Define theme values in one place.
- For the approved UIR presentation, use the exact prototype CSS/geometry from
  `design/future-editor/visual/`; `tokens.css` is the only source of its values.
  Do not import old theme/next/rich styles into the UIR entry; map old semantic
  names in separate `aliases.css`. Use Tailwind theme/utilities without Preflight
  if needed. Follow the UIR execution contract's import graph and engine-control
  overrides; prototype globals must not break menus, handles, icons or focus.
  Native dialog/showModal and nonmodal rewrite show are allowed; do not add a
  Radix Dialog Portal/focus trap. Engine-owned DOM may use a narrow adapter.
- The adopted rich UI is light-only, including its assistant. This supersedes
  earlier light/dark/system requirements in the AG plan and AG07 contract for
  the new presentation; keep their historical evidence unchanged. Remove old
  theme bootstraps from both rich HTML entries in UIR02, detach rich theme
  listeners and remove the Settings theme selector. Set root `color-scheme: light`
  on the proof and adopted entries. Keep the legacy entry/theme/specs until
  UIR09 separately audits their consumers and test mappings.
- Use complete Tailwind class names or explicit variant maps; do not construct
  class fragments dynamically.

# TypeScript standards

- Apply these rules to application code, tests, and generated project contracts.
- Enable `strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`,
  `noImplicitOverride`, and `noFallthroughCasesInSwitch` in every TS project.
- Do not use explicit or implicit `any`. Receive untyped external data as
  `unknown`, validate it, then narrow it before use.
- Do not declare `enum` or `const enum`. Use literal unions or `as const` objects.
- Example: `type SaveState = "saved" | "pending" | "failed"`.
- Do not use `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-nocheck`, double assertions, or lint suppressions
  to bypass these rules. Keep legitimate negative type tests separate.
- Configure contract generation to emit literal unions rather than enum declarations.
- At frontend setup, add `tsc --noEmit` and type-aware ESLint to local checks and CI.
- Enforce `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any` and the no-unsafe assignment,
  argument, call, member-access, and return rules as errors.
- Use `no-restricted-syntax` with `TSEnumDeclaration` to ban both enum forms.
